From 673faac7ce0a091484418fe48edee0c33e61552b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abinash Haldorai <abinash.haldorai@eka.care>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:27:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Console: register a phone number, connect it to an agent,
 and set up handover

Phone numbers (channel telephony, provider vobiz) could only be created
through the API. Add the console pages:

- New Integration offers "Phone number"; its form takes the number to
  answer and, optionally, the clinic's own number that forwards to it. The
  number is validated (country code) and normalised; a number already
  registered says so. What was typed stays on the form after an error.
- The number's page shows the Answer URL to paste into Vobiz, and offers the
  agent only (a phone number is not a WhatsApp inbox, so Messenger and the
  status callback are hidden, and the server refuses Messenger for it).
- A "Hand over to a person" section on that page: staff phone number, staff
  hours (start, end, timezone; empty = always) and ring time, stored as the
  binding's handover config. Saving a form that has no such section (a
  WhatsApp number's) leaves a stored handover alone.
- A line pointing to the agent's page, where voice, language and greeting
  already live.

Not in this change: a test-call button, the call list, or a "text the
clinic" fallback. theme/static/css/dist/styles.css is the tracked Tailwind
build and is not regenerated here (the Dockerfile builds it); run
`python manage.py tailwind build` if the repo wants it refreshed.

Tests render the real templates with a bare base layout and run without a
database. Checked by eye in a browser from the rendered pages; not run
against the live console.

